<div class="notice">IMPORTANT: THIS SERVICE CONTRACT IS NOT AN INSURANCE POLICY.</div>
<p>This Document constitutes a Service Contract administered by A-Protect Warranty Corporation. Any authorization, payment, benefit, reimbursement, or service provided hereunder shall be subject exclusively to the terms, conditions, limitations, exclusions, and eligibility requirements set forth in this Service Contract. This Service Contract does not constitute a policy of insurance, does not provide indemnity against loss, and does not provide collision, comprehensive, liability, or any other form of automobile insurance coverage. It is not intended to replace, supplement, or satisfy any insurance coverage required by applicable law.</p>
<h2 class="part">PART 1: DEFINITIONS</h2>
<p>Under this Service Contract, the following words will denote the meanings set forth below:</p>
<p class="def">“A-Protect” means A-Protect Warranty Corporation, the administrator and service provider of this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="def">“Service Contract” means the A-Protect Service Contract, which includes all Terms and Conditions, the Registration Page, the Application, and any addenda or amendments issued by A-Protect and accepted by the Customer.</p>
<p class="def">“A-Protect Authorized Repair Facility” refers to the repair facilities designated and directly authorized by A-Protect to perform repairs and services on the Registered Vehicle as required under A-Protect Service Contract programs.</p>
<p class="def">“Claim” means a customer service request for review and authorization of repairs to eligible components under this Service Contract. All claim handling performed by A-Protect is administrative in nature and does not constitute the payment of insurance benefits.</p>
<p class="def">“Commercial Use” means any vehicle primarily used to generate income, perform services for compensation, transport goods or passengers for hire, or support business operations beyond incidental use. Commercial Use includes, but is not limited to: Ride-share, taxi, limousine, or driving instruction/Food, courier, or parcel delivery/Fleet or rental operations/Construction, industrial, oilfield, agricultural, or municipal service/ Snow plowing/ Commercial hauling or towing for compensation. A vehicle may be classified as Commercial Use based on its actual operation, frequency of use, average monthly mileage, equipment installed, or purpose of operation, regardless of registration status. Incidental business use (such as occasional travel between job sites or transporting tools not exceeding manufacturer payload limits) does not automatically constitute Commercial Use. Final classification of vehicle use shall be determined by A-Protect based on manufacturer specifications and documented usage patterns.</p>
<p class="def">“Light-Duty Usage” means the vehicle is used primarily for personal transportation or ordinary business activities that do not involve carrying passengers or property for compensation, towing beyond manufacturer recommendations, or operating in severe commercial service. (driving up to 30,000 kms a year)</p>
<p class="def">“Medium-Duty Usage” means a vehicle with a Gross Vehicle Weight Rating (GVWR) between 8,501 lbs and 14,000 lbs that is used for business or commercial purposes but is not engaged in heavy-duty hauling, long-haul transportation, mining, logging, emergency services, or other severe-duty operations.</p>
<p class="def">“Heavy-Duty Vehicle” means a vehicle with a GVWR exceeding 14,000 lbs that is used for commercial, industrial, transportation, construction, agricultural, municipal, or other severe-duty operations.</p>
<p class="def">“Customer” means the Registered Vehicle Owner or Purchaser identified on the A-Protect Vehicle Service Contract Application and Registration Page to which this Service Contract pertains.</p>
<p class="def">“Mechanical Breakdown” means the sudden and accidental failure of a covered component due to defects in materials or workmanship, resulting in the component’s inability to perform its intended function.</p>
<p class="def">“Pre-existing Condition(s)” means any mechanical failure, defect, or operating problem that existed before the purchase date.</p>
<p class="def">“Selling Dealer” means the authorized retailer, dealership, or other duly authorized person through whom the Customer purchases the Service Contract.</p>
<p class="def">“Unlimited Kilometres” Unlimited kilometres apply for the duration of the warranty term.</p>
<h2 class="part">PART 2: EXTENDED LIMITED WARRANTY SERVICE AGREEMENT</h2>
<p>This Service Contract provides mechanical breakdown service administration solely for the Registered Vehicle identified on the Application and Registration Page. Coverage applies only to the Coverage Plan and any optional benefits or additional coverage expressly selected and identified on the Application and Registration Page. Within the selected Coverage Plan, only those components and services specifically identified as covered under the applicable provisions of this Service Contract are eligible for authorization. All coverage is subject to the terms, conditions, eligibility requirements, limitations, exclusions, deductibles, maximum authorized repair limits, and Claims Procedures set forth in this Service Contract. Any component, repair, service, benefit, or option that is not expressly included within the selected Coverage Plan or identified as an applicable additional option is not covered and will not be eligible for authorization, reimbursement, or payment by A-Protect. No representation, description, brochure, advertisement, verbal statement, or other communication shall modify or expand the coverage provided under this Service Contract unless expressly incorporated into the Service Contract by a written addendum, endorsement, or amendment issued or approved by A-Protect.</p>
<h2 class="part">PART 3: COVERED PARTS AND OPTIONS</h2>
<p>Program Selected: Refer to the Application Page for the Coverage Plan, term, deductible, per-claim limit and any optional coverages selected. The following parts, components, benefits, and services are covered only where they are included within the Coverage Plan selected by the Customer or have been separately selected as an optional coverage and identified on the Application or Registration Page. The inclusion of any part, component, benefit, or service within this section does not, by itself, establish coverage. Coverage applies only where the applicable item is included in the Customer’s selected Coverage Plan or expressly identified as an additional selected option, and remains subject to all applicable terms, conditions, limitations, exclusions, and eligibility requirements of this Service Contract.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">ENGINE</h4>
<p class="sub">Applies only to internally lubricated parts</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Engine block; crankshaft; pistons; piston rings when broken as a result of a covered Mechanical Breakdown; connecting rods and bearings; wrist pins; cylinder heads; camshaft and camshaft bearings; engine main bearings; rocker arm assemblies; intake and exhaust valves; valve guides; valve lifters and pushrods; valve springs and retainers; sprockets and related gears; timing belt (covered only when replacement is required in connection with an authorized repair to another covered Engine component; not covered as a standalone repair or maintenance item); timing chain and tensioners (covered only following a verified Mechanical Breakdown; not covered for stretching, noise, preventative replacement, maintenance-related replacement, or where no Mechanical Breakdown has occurred); internal variable timing components; engine oil pump; and other internally lubricated Engine components contained within the Engine assembly.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Rust; corrosion; overheating damage arising from any cause; oil filter housing; oil cooler; valve cover; worn piston rings resulting in oil consumption; seized piston rings; worn bearings that have not experienced a Mechanical Breakdown; and normal Wear and Tear unless Wear and Tear Coverage is expressly included in the selected Coverage Plan.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">TRANSMISSION</h4>
<p class="sub">Applies only to internally lubricated parts</p>
<p class="num">1. Automatic Transmission: Transmission case, gear sets, input and output shafts, torque converter, solenoid packs, valve body, accumulator, fluid pump, countershaft, modulator valve (if applicable), bearings, bands, band apply servo, parking pawl.</p>
<p class="num">2. Manual Transmission: Transmission housing, bearings, input and output shafts, countershaft, synchro assemblies, gear sets, selector shaft, shifter forks.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Manual clutch components, external linkages, flex plate, fly wheels, transmission control module (TCM), and reprogramming.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">DIFFERENTIAL</h4>
<p class="num">1. Front Wheel Drive (FWD): Housing, bearings, crown and pinion.</p>
<p class="num">2. Rear Wheel Drive (RWD): Housing, carrier gear and case, driver pinion and pinion gear, ring gear, differential cover, differential bearings, viscous couplers.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">TRANSFER CASE/4X4</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Auxiliary differential and transfer case housing (including gears, sprockets, and internal bearings).</p>
<h4 class="cmp">TURBO/SUPERCHARGER</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Turbo/supercharger assembly and housing, supercharger compressor, turbo internal bearings and lubricated parts, turbine wheels, turbine housing, clutch and pulley, wastegate and wastegate actuator, wastegate linkage, wastegate controller, blow-off valve, diverter valve, mechanical pressure release valve, bypass valve, intercooler, turbo/supercharger water pump.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">TOWING</h4>
<p>A-Protect will reimburse the Customer up to $60.00 per authorized repair for towing expenses incurred due to covered mechanical failure. Valid receipts must be provided at the time of the claim.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">TRIP INTERRUPTION</h4>
<p>For covered repairs, A-Protect will reimburse the Customer up to the maximum $150.00 for lodging, meals, bus, or taxi. If the authorized repair facility is unable to provide same-day service and is further away than 200 km (one-way) from the Customer’s home. Valid receipts must be provided within 7 days of the occurrence to be eligible for reimbursement.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">AIR CONDITIONING</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> A/C compressor, A/C compressor clutch assembly, A/C condenser, evaporator core, expansion valve, receiver/dryer, accumulator, orifice tube, A/C seals and gaskets (within covered components), A/C lines, Schrader valves.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Freon and recharge.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">BRAKES</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Master cylinder, brake calipers, brake vacuum booster, wheel cylinders, brake flex hoses, hydraulic steel lines and fittings, proportioning valve.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> ABS pump.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">COOLING SYSTEM</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Water pump, radiator, radiator cooling fan (electric/mechanical), auxiliary water pump, heater core, coolant reservoir (overflow/compression tank), heater control valve, cooling fan clutch (mechanical).</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Hoses, clamps, coolant, and reservoirs.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">ELECTRICAL</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Alternator, starter motor, starter motor solenoid, alternator voltage regulator, windshield washer pump (front &amp; rear), heater fan, electrical air conditioning condenser fan motor, horn assembly, electric radiator fan, motor &amp; assembly, windshield wiper motor (front &amp; rear).</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> ABS sensor.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">FRONT SUSPENSION</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Control arms (upper and lower), control arm bushings, ball joints (upper and lower), steering knuckles.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Struts, shocks, springs, sway bars and links, mounts, wheel hubs, and any other suspension component not specifically listed above.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">REAR SUSPENSION</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Control arms (upper and lower), control arm bushings, ball joints (upper and lower).</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Struts, shocks, springs, sway bars and links, sway bar mounts, wheel hubs, and any other suspension component not specifically listed above.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">FUEL SYSTEM</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Fuel injectors, fuel injector lines, fuel pressure regulator, fuel pump, direct injection fuel pump, fuel rails, fuel gauge sender (sending unit), fuel tank.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">HYBRID COMPONENTS</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Hybrid control module, inverter, hybrid electric motor(s)/ generator/ drive unit, hybrid specific transaxle and transmission housing, voltage inverter module, battery control module, battery pack cooling fan, DC/DC converter, onboard charger, and fan.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Battery.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">POWER STEERING</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Power steering pump (including its seals and gaskets), rack and pinion (including its seals and gaskets), manual and power steering box, electric power assist motor.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Clock spring.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">SEALS &amp; GASKETS</h4>
<p>Internal seals and gaskets used to contain fluids/lubricants within the covered parts only when required in connection with the repair or replacement of a covered internally lubricated component listed in this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Crankshaft seal (front and rear), camshaft seals, cylinder head gaskets, oil pan gasket, timing cover gasket, valve cover gasket, intake manifold gaskets, valve guide seals, transmission/transaxle seals and gaskets, transfer case seals and gaskets, differential seals and gaskets.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Axle seals.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">SUPPLEMENTARY PARTS</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Motor mounts, oil pan, harmonic balancer, intake and exhaust manifold, timing cover, oil pressure sending unit, temperature gauge sending unit, dipstick and tube, flywheel, engine cooling fan clutch and assembly, drive shafts &amp; universal joints, wheel bearings, CV axle shafts, cv joints and boots, transfer case mounts, transmission mounts, differential mounts, torque struts, hanger bearings, flex plate and flywheel ring/gear.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">WEAR &amp; TEAR</h4>
<p>Wear and Tear is not covered under this Service Contract unless expressly included in the specific coverage package selected on the front page of the application. Where Wear and Tear Coverage is included, it applies only to a factory-installed covered powertrain component specifically listed under the selected coverage package that has failed due to normal wear arising from ordinary use of the vehicle and has experienced a complete mechanical breakdown, rendering the component incapable of performing its intended function.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Wear and Tear Coverage does not apply to gradual deterioration that has not resulted in complete mechanical breakdown, reduced performance, noise, vibration, minor seepage or leakage, carbon buildup, components operating within or exceeding manufacturer tolerances without actual failure, or parts recommended for replacement as part of routine maintenance, including but not limited to tires, brake friction materials and linings, clutch friction materials, belts, hoses, filters, fluids, batteries, spark plugs, light bulbs, and wiper blades.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">ROADSIDE COVERAGE – REIMBURSEMENT ONLY</h4>
<p>Roadside Coverage applies exclusively to the Registered Vehicle. The Customer is responsible for arranging roadside assistance through a third-party provider. A- Protect does not dispatch roadside service providers or arrange transportation of the Registered Vehicle. Eligible roadside services include towing, fuel delivery (excluding the cost of fuel), battery boost, lockout service (excluding locksmith charges), tire change using the vehicle’s available spare tire, and winching. A-Protect will reimburse the Customer up to $75.00 per occurrence, subject to a maximum aggregate reimbursement of $225.00 for the entire term of this Service Contract. Valid receipts and proof of payment must be submitted to A-Protect within fourteen (14) days of the occurrence to qualify for reimbursement.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">CAR RENTAL – REIMBURSEMENT ONLY</h4>
<p>In the event of a covered Mechanical Breakdown, where the authorized repairs require more than one (1) business day to complete, A-Protect will reimburse the Customer for eligible car rental expenses incurred, up to a maximum of $60.00 per day, subject to an aggregate maximum reimbursement of $300.00 for the entire term of this Service Contract. Reimbursement is subject to the submission of valid receipts and proof of payment at the time of the Claim.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">HI-TECH COMPONENTS</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Electronic instrument displays (speedometer, tachometer, odometer, fuel, oil, temperature, voltage), collision avoidance system sensors &amp; modules, adaptive cruise control components, display &amp; screen (including navigation, climate control &amp; media settings), GPS control module, power window motors, power door lock actuator motors, power seat motor, power sliding door motor, power window regulators, power window switches, blind spot monitoring sensors, cameras (front/rear/side), entertainment systems (radio/dvd/cd), exterior mirror motors, heated mirrors, heated seat components, heated steering wheel components, lane assist/collision avoidance system components, lift gate motor, parking assist sensors (front/rear), power mirror controllers.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">HI-TECH ELITE</h4>
<p class="lead"><b>Includes:</b> Electronic instrument displays (speedometer, tachometer, odometer, fuel, oil, temperature, voltage), collision avoidance system sensors &amp; modules, adaptive cruise control components, display &amp; screen (including navigation, climate control &amp; media settings), Bluetooth voice activation control module, GPS control module, power window motors, power door lock actuator motors, power seat motor, power sliding door motor, power window regulators, power window switches, blind spot monitoring sensors, bluetooth voice activation control module, cameras (front/rear/side), entertainment systems (radio/DVD/cd), exterior mirror motors, heated mirrors, heated seat components, heated steering wheel, lane assist/collision avoidance system components, lift gate motor, parking assist sensors (front/rear), power mirror controllers, anti-theft control module, auto lights sensors, auto wiper sensors, body/power control module, centre console lock actuators, child safety door lock mechanisms, convertible top motor, cruise control radar distance sensor, daytime running lights module, door keypad receiver, electric hood release actuator motor, electric trunk release actuator motor, glove box lock actuators, ignition switch, interior manually operated electrical switches (including ignition switch), keyless entry door handle sensor, keyless entry door keypad, keyless entry receiver, power antenna motor, sunroof motor, tailgate activation sensor, tire pressure warning control module (TPMS), wi-fi control module.</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Exclusions:</b> Wiring harness.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">POWERTRAIN PLUS</h4>
<p class="num">1. Engine Management: Electronic control module (ECM); powertrain control module (PCM); engine management sensors; fuel injection management sensors; idle air control module and valve; and engine wiring harness.</p>
<p class="num">2. 4X4/Drivetrain: 4x4 locking hubs; electronic and vacuum-operated transfer case and differential engagement components; transfer case control module; transmission control module; and transmission wiring harness.</p>
<p class="num">3. Suspension &amp; Safety Systems: Front and rear air ride/load-levelling compressors; air ride/load-levelling control module; airbag module and controllers; ABS pump and pressure modulator assembly; anti-lock brake sensor rings; and anti-lock brake/traction control module.</p>
<p class="num">4. Sensors: Crankshaft sensors; camshaft sensors; knock sensor; NOx sensors; oxygen sensors; mass air flow sensors; manifold absolute pressure (MAP) sensor; and wheel speed sensors.</p>
<p class="num">5. Emission Control: EVAP emission control components; PCV valve; purge canister; and purge solenoid.</p>
<p class="num">6. Ignition &amp; intake components: Electronic ignition components; ignition coils and coil packs; throttle body and actuators; and intake manifold actuators.</p>
<h4 class="cmp">UNLIMITED KM OPTION</h4>
<p>If the Unlimited Kilometres option is selected on the Application and Registration Page, the Service Contract term shall be governed solely by the time period (months or years) shown and shall not be subject to a kilometre limit. Unlimited Kilometres coverage is available only for vehicles used for personal use or approved light-duty commercial use, with annual usage not exceeding 30,000 kilometres throughout the term of the Service Contract. Vehicles exceeding 30,000 kilometres per year, or used for Commercial, Business, Fleet, Delivery, Ride-Share, Rental, Taxi, Emergency Services, or other high-mileage or commercial operations, are not eligible for Unlimited Kilometres coverage. If A-Protect determines, based on reasonable evidence of the vehicle's actual use, that the eligibility requirements are not met, the Service Contract may be reclassified to the corresponding kilometre-limited plan for the same time term (for example, a 48-Month Unlimited Kilometres plan may be converted to a 48-Month/80,000 km plan).</p>

